Don't force hidden visibility for the ONNX C++ library.

ONNX Runtime uses functions such as DataTypeUtils::ToType and OpSchema::Attr
that are not annotated with ONNX_API. Forcing hidden visibility makes these
symbols unavailable from libonnx.so, causing undefined references when linking
against system ONNX. Remove the target's visibility override so the build's
default visibility settings apply.

--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -530,7 +530,6 @@
 add_library(onnx $<TARGET_OBJECTS:onnx_proto>)
 add_subdirectory(onnx)
 add_dependencies(onnx onnx_proto)
-set_target_properties(onnx PROPERTIES CXX_VISIBILITY_PRESET hidden)
 add_onnx_global_defines(onnx)
 if(ONNX_BUILD_PYTHON)
   if(BUILD_SHARED_LIBS)
